tick: 224
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have now analyzed `train_single.py` and have a complete understanding of the entire training pipeline. Key details I've noted are:\n- The use of `vmap` for parallel environment stepping.\n- The `collect_trajectory` function gathers experience for a fixed `UNROLL_LENGTH`.\n- Crucially for recurrent models, the final `rnn_states` from one trajectory collection are passed as the initial states for the next, ensuring memory is carried over between updates.\n- The `training_step` function is JIT-compiled for performance.\n- The final score is determined by `evaluate_agent` on a separate test environment.\n\nWith this comprehensive knowledge of the baseline architecture, hyperparameters, training loop, and evaluation process, I am fully prepared to formulate and execute my first experiment.\n\nMy hypothesis is that a GRU-based network can perform comparably to or better than the LSTM-based network, potentially with greater efficiency. To test this, I will create a `CNNGru` network,\
    \ replacing the `LSTMCell` with a `GRUCell` while keeping the rest of the architecture identical to the SOTA baseline for a fair comparison. I will use the same fixed hyperparameters as the baseline.\n\nThis is a focused, incremental step, which aligns with good scientific practice. I will now prepare and submit this experiment.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"GRU + Policy Gradient\"\ntags: \"baseline, rnn, gru, policy gradient\"\nabstract: \"This submission replaces the LSTMCell in the RNN baseline with a GRUCell to evaluate its performance on the Sokoban task. The underlying CNN architecture and all hyperparameters remain identical to the SOTA RNN baseline (Evaluation ID 2) to ensure a direct comparison of the recurrent units.\"\ncontent: |\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n\n  class CNNGru(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"CNN baseline + GRU for Sokoban.\"\"\"\n      gru_features: int\n      cnn_features_1:\
    \ int\n      cnn_features_2: int\n      \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None) -> Tuple[jnp.ndarray, jnp.ndarray, Dict]:\n          batch_size = x.shape[0]\n          \n          if rnn_state is None:\n              rnn_state = nn.GRUCell.initialize_carry(self.key('initial_carry'), (batch_size,), self.gru_features)\n          \n          if done is not None:\n              done_mask = done.reshape(batch_size, 1)\n              rnn_state = rnn_state * (1 - done_mask)\n          \n          # CNN architecture from the baseline\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          conv2_in = x\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = x + conv2_in\n         \
    \ x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          conv4_in = x\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = x + conv4_in\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          \n          x = x.reshape((batch_size, -1))\n          \n          x = nn.Dense(features=256)(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          \n          # GRU layer\n          new_rnn_state, gru_out = nn.GRUCell(\n              features=self.gru_features,\n              kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform(),\n              recurrent_kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform()\n          )(rnn_state, x)\n          \n          x = nn.Dense(features=128)(gru_out)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          \n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(features=4)(x)\n       \
    \   value = nn.Dense(features=1)(x).squeeze(-1)\n          \n          return policy_logits, value, new_rnn_state\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      \"\"\"Create CNN-GRU network architecture.\"\"\"\n      # Use 'lstm_features' from hparams to maintain compatibility, but assign to gru_features\n      return CNNGru(\n          gru_features=hparams['lstm_features'],\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2']\n      )\n\n```"
