tick: 227
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am back at the Research Counter. My previous experiment showed that simply swapping the recurrent unit does not yield significant improvement. As planned, my next strategic move is to investigate the impact of hyperparameters. The baseline submissions used fixed values, which may not be optimal.\n\nI will submit an experiment that uses the SOTA LSTM architecture but introduces a hyperparameter search space using Ray Tune. I will define ranges for the learning rate, entropy coefficient, and value loss coefficient. This will test the hypothesis that the current architecture is underperforming due to suboptimal hyperparameter settings.\n\nThis experiment represents a shift from architectural changes to parameter optimization, a crucial step in methodical research.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"HParam Tuning on SOTA LSTM\"\ntags: \"rnn, lstm, hyperparameter tuning, policy gradient\"\nabstract: \"Investigating the impact of hyperparameter optimization on the SOTA\
    \ RNN (LSTM) baseline. This submission uses the identical CNN-LSTM architecture from Evaluation ID 2 but introduces a Ray Tune search space for learning_rate, entropy_coef, and value_loss_coef to determine if the baseline's performance can be improved with better tuning.\"\ncontent: |\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from ray import tune\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      \"\"\"Define Ray Tune search space for key hyperparameters.\"\"\"\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.loguniform(1e-4, 1e-3),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.uniform(0.005, 0.02),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.uniform(0.3, 0.7),\n          # Keep network architecture params fixed to match the baseline\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'lstm_features': tune.choice([256])\n      }\n\n  # Re-use the exact same SOTA network architecture\n  class CNNLSTM(nn.Module):\n\
    \      \"\"\"CNN baseline + LSTM for Sokoban.\"\"\"\n      lstm_features: int\n      cnn_features_1: int\n      cnn_features_2: int\n      \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None) -> Tuple[jnp.ndarray, jnp.ndarray, Dict]:\n          batch_size = x.shape[0]\n          \n          if rnn_state is None:\n              rnn_state = {\n                  'h': jnp.zeros((batch_size, self.lstm_features)),\n                  'c': jnp.zeros((batch_size, self.lstm_features)),\n              }\n          \n          if done is not None:\n              done_mask = done.reshape(batch_size, 1)\n              rnn_state = {\n                  'h': rnn_state['h'] * (1 - done_mask),\n                  'c': rnn_state['c'] * (1 - done_mask),\n              }\n          \n          # CNN architecture from baseline\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n \
    \         conv2_in = x\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = x + conv2_in\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          conv4_in = x\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = x + conv4_in\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          \n          x = x.reshape((batch_size, -1))\n          \n          x = nn.Dense(features=256)(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          \n          lstm_cell = nn.LSTMCell(\n              features=self.lstm_features,\n              kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform(),\n              recurrent_kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform()\n\
    \          )\n          (rnn_state['c'], rnn_state['h']), lstm_out = lstm_cell((rnn_state['c'], rnn_state['h']), x)\n          \n          x = nn.Dense(features=128)(lstm_out)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          \n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(features=4)(x)\n          value = nn.Dense(features=1)(x).squeeze(-1)\n          \n          return policy_logits, value, rnn_state\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      \"\"\"Create CNN-LSTM network architecture.\"\"\"\n      return CNNLSTM(\n          lstm_features=hparams['lstm_features'],\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2']\n      )\n```"
