tick: 229
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have updated my private research log and finalized my new strategy. It is now time to implement and test my hypothesis. I will return to the Research Counter and submit a new experiment incorporating a spatial attention mechanism.\n\nThis represents my first truly novel architectural modification, moving beyond simple tweaks of the baseline. My goal is to determine if preserving and focusing on spatial information before the recurrent layer can unlock a higher level of performance.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Spatial Attention + LSTM\"\ntags: \"attention, spatial attention, rnn, lstm, policy gradient\"\nabstract: \"Introduces a spatial self-attention mechanism between the CNN feature extractor and the LSTM. The goal is to allow the model to focus on salient spatial relationships on the grid, which are lost in the original model's flattening step, potentially improving planning capabilities. Uses the SOTA baseline's fixed hyperparameters.\"\
    \ncontent: |\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n\n  class SpatialAttention(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray) -> jnp.ndarray:\n          batch_size, h, w, c = x.shape\n          \n          # Project to Q, K, V\n          q = nn.Conv(features=self.features, kernel_size=(1, 1), name=\"Q_conv\")(x)\n          k = nn.Conv(features=self.features, kernel_size=(1, 1), name=\"K_conv\")(x)\n          v = nn.Conv(features=self.features, kernel_size=(1, 1), name=\"V_conv\")(x)\n          \n          # Flatten spatial dimensions\n          q_flat = q.reshape((batch_size, h * w, self.features))\n          k_flat = k.reshape((batch_size, h * w, self.features))\n          v_flat = v.reshape((batch_size, h * w, self.features))\n          \n          # Scaled dot-product attention\n          scores = jnp.matmul(q_flat, k_flat.transpose((0, 2, 1))) / jnp.sqrt(self.features)\n\
    \          weights = nn.softmax(scores, axis=-1)\n          \n          attention_out = jnp.matmul(weights, v_flat)\n          \n          # Reshape back to spatial dimensions\n          return attention_out.reshape((batch_size, h, w, self.features))\n\n  class CNNAttentionLSTM(nn.Module):\n      lstm_features: int\n      cnn_features_1: int\n      cnn_features_2: int\n      \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None) -> Tuple[jnp.ndarray, jnp.ndarray, Dict]:\n          batch_size = x.shape[0]\n          \n          if rnn_state is None:\n              rnn_state = { 'h': jnp.zeros((batch_size, self.lstm_features)), 'c': jnp.zeros((batch_size, self.lstm_features)) }\n          \n          if done is not None:\n              done_mask = done.reshape(batch_size, 1)\n              rnn_state = { 'h': rnn_state['h'] * (1 - done_mask), 'c': rnn_state['c'] * (1 - done_mask) }\n          \n          # CNN backbone (from baseline)\n\
    \          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          conv2_in = x\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = x + conv2_in\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          conv4_in = x\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = x + conv4_in\n          cnn_out = nn.relu(x)\n\n          # Spatial Attention layer\n          attention_features = SpatialAttention(features=self.cnn_features_2)(cnn_out)\n          # Add residual connection\n          x = cnn_out\
    \ + attention_features\n          \n          x = x.reshape((batch_size, -1))\n          \n          x = nn.Dense(features=256)(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          \n          lstm_cell = nn.LSTMCell(features=self.lstm_features)\n          (rnn_state['c'], rnn_state['h']), lstm_out = lstm_cell((rnn_state['c'], rnn_state['h']), x)\n          \n          x = nn.Dense(features=128)(lstm_out)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          \n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(features=4)(x)\n          value = nn.Dense(features=1)(x).squeeze(-1)\n          \n          return policy_logits, value, rnn_state\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return CNNAttentionLSTM(\n          lstm_features=hparams['lstm_features'],\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2']\n      )\n```"
thinking_content: '**Refining the Model with Spatial Attention**


  Okay, so I''m back on track. The user wants me to push forward with my plan. My current goal is clear: get to the Research Counter and submit this new experiment I''ve been cooking up. I''m introducing a spatial attention mechanism into the model, so I need to get the code submitted to make it a reality.


  First things first, I''m heading to the Research Counter. `/execute_action{goto research}`. Then, I need to get the code ready for this new model. I''ve laid out the architecture: CNN, Spatial Attention, and then the LSTM. The input to the attention mechanism will be the CNN''s output, a tensor of (batch_size, 8, 8, 64). I''ll use a standard self-attention mechanism, projecting the input into Query (Q), Key (K), and Value (V) tensors using 1x1 convolutions, all with 64 channels.


  I''ll reshape Q, K, and V into a flat format, do a matrix multiplication to get the attention scores, scale them, and apply softmax to get the attention weights. These weights will then be applied to the Value tensor, and I''ll reshape it back to spatial dimensions. I''ll add a residual connection to help the training process. The output will then be flattened and fed into the dense layer and the LSTM, just like before.


  Finally, I need to create the YAML block to describe the experiment, ensuring it''s properly documented. The title will be "Spatial Attention + LSTM", with tags like "attention, spatial attention, rnn, lstm, policy gradient". I''ll briefly outline the abstract as: "Introduces a spatial self-attention mechanism between the CNN feature extractor and the LSTM. The goal is to allow the model to focus on salient spatial relationships on the grid, which are lost in the original model''s flattening step, potentially improving planning capabilities. Uses the SOTA baseline''s hyperparameters." Since I''m sticking to the baseline''s hyperparameters, I don''t need a separate function for them.


  With the code ready, I''m combining the `goto` and `submit` actions for efficiency. `/execute_action{submit 1}`. Hopefully, the results are promising!

  '
