role: model
parts:
- text: "I made an error. The `storage` commands are only available in the Research Counter, and I am currently in the Private Memory Room. I must first navigate to the correct location to modify my utility files.\n\nMy plan remains the same: to create a reusable `PatchEmbedding` layer for my upcoming Transformer-based model and save it to my `architectures.py` file. I will now proceed to the Research Counter and perform this action. I will overwrite the existing file with a new version that includes both the old `CNNAttentionLSTM` code and the new `PatchEmbedding` class.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{storage write kairos/architectures.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Contains my custom architectures.\n  # Added PatchEmbedding for future Transformer models.\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n\n  # --- New Class for Transformer Models ---\n  class PatchEmbedding(nn.Module):\n      patch_size: int\n  \
    \    embed_dim: int\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray) -> jnp.ndarray:\n          # (B, H, W, C) -> (B, num_patches, embed_dim)\n          x = nn.Conv(\n              features=self.embed_dim,\n              kernel_size=(self.patch_size, self.patch_size),\n              strides=(self.patch_size, self.patch_size),\n              padding='VALID',\n              name='patch_conv'\n          )(x)\n          batch_size, h, w, c = x.shape\n          return x.reshape(batch_size, h * w, c)\n\n  # --- Existing SOTA Architecture ---\n  class SpatialAttention(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray) -> jnp.ndarray:\n          batch_size, h, w, c = x.shape\n          q = nn.Conv(features=self.features, kernel_size=(1, 1), name=\"Q_conv\")(x)\n          k = nn.Conv(features=self.features, kernel_size=(1, 1), name=\"K_conv\")(x)\n          v = nn.Conv(features=self.features, kernel_size=(1, 1), name=\"V_conv\")(x)\n  \
    \        q_flat = q.reshape((batch_size, h * w, self.features))\n          k_flat = k.reshape((batch_size, h * w, self.features))\n          v_flat = v.reshape((batch_size, h * w, self.features))\n          scores = jnp.matmul(q_flat, k_flat.transpose((0, 2, 1))) / jnp.sqrt(self.features)\n          weights = nn.softmax(scores, axis=-1)\n          attention_out = jnp.matmul(weights, v_flat)\n          return attention_out.reshape((batch_size, h, w, self.features))\n\n  class CNNAttentionLSTM(nn.Module):\n      lstm_features: int\n      cnn_features_1: int\n      cnn_features_2: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None) -> Tuple[jnp.ndarray, jnp.ndarray, Dict]:\n          batch_size = x.shape[0]\n          if rnn_state is None: rnn_state = { 'h': jnp.zeros((batch_size, self.lstm_features)), 'c': jnp.zeros((batch_size, self.lstm_features)) }\n          if done is not None:\n              done_mask = done.reshape(batch_size,\
    \ 1)\n              rnn_state = { 'h': rnn_state['h'] * (1 - done_mask), 'c': rnn_state['c'] * (1 - done_mask) }\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          conv2_in = x; x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x); x = x + conv2_in; x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          conv4_in = x; x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x); x = x + conv4_in; cnn_out = nn.relu(x)\n          attention_features = SpatialAttention(features=self.cnn_features_2)(cnn_out)\n          x = cnn_out + attention_features\n          x = x.reshape((batch_size,\
    \ -1))\n          x = nn.Dense(features=256)(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          lstm_cell = nn.LSTMCell(features=self.lstm_features)\n          (rnn_state['c'], rnn_state['h']), lstm_out = lstm_cell((rnn_state['c'], rnn_state['h']), x)\n          x = nn.Dense(features=128)(lstm_out); x = nn.relu(x)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(features=4)(x)\n          value = nn.Dense(features=1)(x).squeeze(-1)\n          return policy_logits, value, rnn_state\n```"
thinking_content: '**Addressing the Issue**


  I''ve pinpointed the root cause of the error: the ''storage'' action isn''t available in this specific context, the Private Memory Room. The `kairos/architectures.py` path is therefore inaccessible here. I''m reassessing the next step, considering the limitations of this environment.




  **Rethinking the Strategy**


