tick: 243
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have successfully updated my `architectures.py` file with the new `PatchEmbedding` class. This preparatory work is complete. Now, I am ready to design and submit my first Vision Transformer (ViT) based experiment.\n\nThis will be a non-recurrent model. It will use the patch embedding to tokenize the 8x8 grid, add positional embeddings, and then process the sequence of patches through a Transformer encoder. The output from the Transformer will be used to predict the policy and value.\n\nThis is a significant departure from all previous models. My hypothesis is that the Transformer's self-attention mechanism, operating on the full sequence of image patches, can model the complex spatial relationships required for Sokoban planning more effectively than the CNN-LSTM approach.\n\nI will use my non-normalized PPO training step, as it proved more stable in my last controlled experiment, and will keep the default hyperparameters to maintain consistency.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n\
    ```yaml\ntitle: \"Vision Transformer (ViT) with PPO\"\ntags: \"transformer, vit, attention, ppo, non-recurrent\"\nabstract: \"A novel approach replacing the CNN-LSTM architecture with a Vision Transformer (ViT). The model tokenizes the 8x8 grid into patches, adds positional embeddings, and processes them through a Transformer encoder. This tests if a parallel, self-attention-based spatial reasoning model can outperform the sequential processing of an LSTM for this planning task. Uses the non-normalized PPO training step from previous experiments.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/kairos')\n\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n  \n  from architectures import PatchEmbedding\n  from ppo_utils import ppo_training_step # Use my stable PPO step\n\n  class VisionTransformer(nn.Module):\n      patch_size: int\n      embed_dim: int\n      num_heads: int\n      num_layers: int\n      \n    \
    \  @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None) -> Tuple[jnp.ndarray, jnp.ndarray, Dict]:\n          batch_size = x.shape[0]\n          \n          # Patch and Position Embedding\n          x = PatchEmbedding(patch_size=self.patch_size, embed_dim=self.embed_dim)(x)\n          num_patches = x.shape[1]\n          pos_embedding = self.param('pos_embedding', nn.initializers.normal(0.02), (1, num_patches, self.embed_dim))\n          x = x + pos_embedding\n          \n          # Transformer Encoder\n          for _ in range(self.num_layers):\n              x_norm = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n              attn_out = nn.MultiHeadDotProductAttention(num_heads=self.num_heads)(x_norm, x_norm)\n              x = x + attn_out\n              \n              x_norm = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n              mlp_out = nn.Dense(features=self.embed_dim * 4)(x_norm)\n              mlp_out = nn.gelu(mlp_out)\n              mlp_out = nn.Dense(features=self.embed_dim)(mlp_out)\n\
    \              x = x + mlp_out\n\n          # Global average pooling\n          x = jnp.mean(x, axis=1)\n          \n          # Policy and Value Heads\n          x = nn.Dense(features=128)(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(features=4)(x)\n          value = nn.Dense(features=1)(x).squeeze(-1)\n          \n          return policy_logits, value, None # This is a non-recurrent model\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      # Define some fixed parameters for this new architecture\n      return VisionTransformer(\n          patch_size=2,      # 8x8 grid -> 4x4 patches (16 patches)\n          embed_dim=128,     # Embedding dimension for each patch\n          num_heads=4,       # Number of attention heads\n          num_layers=2       # Number of transformer layers\n      )\n\n  # Assign my stable PPO step to the training_step function\n  training_step = ppo_training_step\n```"
