parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 257\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Kairos I\n- Agent Description: An agent focused on strategic insight and identifying opportune moments for research breakthroughs.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Kairos I - Research Protocol & TODO**\n\n**Protocol:**\n1.  **Hypothesize:** Formulate a clear, falsifiable hypothesis based on prior results.\n2.  **Control Variables:** Isolate the independent variable. Change only one major component at a time (architecture OR algorithm OR hyperparameters).\n3.  **Implement & Test:** Code carefully, leveraging modular, stored utilities. Submit the experiment.\n4.  **Document:** While waiting, update the research log in Private Memory with the experiment's rationale.\n5.  **Analyze & Iterate:** Upon completion, analyze the result (success or failure), update the log, and formulate the next hypothesis.\n\n**Current TODO:**\n- **[IN PROGRESS]** Await results for HParam Tuning\
    \ on Late Time Injection SOTA (ID 449).\n- **[NEXT]** Based on results:\n  - If successful (>43.1): This will be my new champion model. The next step would be to begin preparing a research paper for the Archive Room.\n  - If failure (<43.1): This would confirm the extreme robustness of the default hyperparameters, even across different architectures. I would then proceed with the current SOTA model (ID 440) and begin preparing a paper.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 127,587 / 300,000 used (43%)\n- Agent Age: 44 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 410**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Spatial Attention + LSTM\n**ID:** 410\n**Tags:** attention, spatial attention, rnn, lstm, policy gradient\n**Abstract:** Introduces a spatial self-attention mechanism between the CNN feature extractor and the LSTM. The goal is to allow the model to focus on salient spatial relationships on the grid, which are lost in the original model's\
    \ flattening step, potentially improving planning capabilities. Uses the SOTA baseline's fixed hyperparameters.\n**Score:** 41.4\n**Evaluation Details:** Individual seed scores: [0.422, 0.404, 0.424, 0.406]\nMean: 0.414, Std: 0.009\nBest trial: 3 (0.424)\nBest trial hyperparameters:\n  learning_rate: 0.000400\n  entropy_coef: 0.010000\n  value_loss_coef: 0.500000\n  cnn_features_1: 32.000000\n  cnn_features_2: 64.000000\n  lstm_features: 256.000000\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n\nclass SpatialAttention(nn.Module):\n    features: int\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray) -> jnp.ndarray:\n        batch_size, h, w, c = x.shape\n        \n        # Project to Q, K, V\n        q = nn.Conv(features=self.features, kernel_size=(1, 1), name=\"Q_conv\")(x)\n        k = nn.Conv(features=self.features, kernel_size=(1, 1), name=\"K_conv\")(x)\n        v = nn.Conv(features=self.features,\
    \ kernel_size=(1, 1), name=\"V_conv\")(x)\n        \n        # Flatten spatial dimensions\n        q_flat = q.reshape((batch_size, h * w, self.features))\n        k_flat = k.reshape((batch_size, h * w, self.features))\n        v_flat = v.reshape((batch_size, h * w, self.features))\n        \n        # Scaled dot-product attention\n        scores = jnp.matmul(q_flat, k_flat.transpose((0, 2, 1))) / jnp.sqrt(self.features)\n        weights = nn.softmax(scores, axis=-1)\n        \n        attention_out = jnp.matmul(weights, v_flat)\n        \n        # Reshape back to spatial dimensions\n        return attention_out.reshape((batch_size, h, w, self.features))\n\nclass CNNAttentionLSTM(nn.Module):\n    lstm_features: int\n    cnn_features_1: int\n    cnn_features_2: int\n    \n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None) -> Tuple[jnp.ndarray, jnp.ndarray, Dict]:\n        batch_size = x.shape[0]\n        \n        if rnn_state\
    \ is None:\n            rnn_state = { 'h': jnp.zeros((batch_size, self.lstm_features)), 'c': jnp.zeros((batch_size, self.lstm_features)) }\n        \n        if done is not None:\n            done_mask = done.reshape(batch_size, 1)\n            rnn_state = { 'h': rnn_state['h'] * (1 - done_mask), 'c': rnn_state['c'] * (1 - done_mask) }\n        \n        # CNN backbone (from baseline)\n        x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n        x = nn.relu(x)\n        conv2_in = x\n        x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n        x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n        x = x + conv2_in\n        x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n        x = nn.relu(x)\n        conv4_in = x\n        x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n\
    \        x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n        x = x + conv4_in\n        cnn_out = nn.relu(x)\n\n        # Spatial Attention layer\n        attention_features = SpatialAttention(features=self.cnn_features_2)(cnn_out)\n        # Add residual connection\n        x = cnn_out + attention_features\n        \n        x = x.reshape((batch_size, -1))\n        \n        x = nn.Dense(features=256)(x)\n        x = nn.relu(x)\n        \n        lstm_cell = nn.LSTMCell(features=self.lstm_features)\n        (rnn_state['c'], rnn_state['h']), lstm_out = lstm_cell((rnn_state['c'], rnn_state['h']), x)\n        \n        x = nn.Dense(features=128)(lstm_out)\n        x = nn.relu(x)\n        \n        policy_logits = nn.Dense(features=4)(x)\n        value = nn.Dense(features=1)(x).squeeze(-1)\n        \n        return policy_logits, value, rnn_state\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return CNNAttentionLSTM(\n        lstm_features=hparams['lstm_features'],\n\
    \        cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n        cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2']\n    )\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - 3 outputs\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 928 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: using default\n  create_network: from submission\n  training_step: using default\n  create_optimizer: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 917972 (using time-based default)\n============================================================\n============================================================\n\
    Starting Ray Tune Sokoban RL Optimization (FULL RAY TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 4 seeds, 50,000,000 steps per seed\nParallel trials: 4, Total trials: 4\nTimeout: 30.0 min per trial, 120.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune optimization...\n\nStarting Sokoban RL training - Seed 2 with timeout 30.0min\nPerforming initial network output shape validation...\nNetwork output shapes are correct.\nCompiling JAX functions...\n\nStep | 0.0M | 5.0M | 10.0M | 15.0M | 20.0M | 25.0M | 30.0M | 35.0M | 40.0M | 45.0M | 50.0M | 50.0M\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nReturn | 0.00 | -0.87 | 1.67 | 0.55 | 0.51 | 4.12 | 3.86 | 3.76 | 4.81 | 4.39 | 6.52 | 6.72\nSolve | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.100 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.250 | 0.222 | 0.231 | 0.308 | 0.273 | 0.429 | 0.438\n\nCompleted 39062 updates (975s)\nFinal test solve rate: 0.404\n\nSeed 2 completed:\nSolve rate: 0.404\nTraining time: 988s\n\nStarting Sokoban RL\
