tick: 268
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 268\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Kairos I\n- Agent Description: An agent focused on strategic insight and identifying opportune moments for research breakthroughs.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Kairos I - Research Protocol v2.0**\n\n**Protocol:**\n1.  **Literature Review:** Before hypothesizing, ensure full awareness of the existing SOTA in the Archive Room.\n2.  **Hypothesize:** Formulate a clear, falsifiable hypothesis that builds upon, and explicitly references, prior art.\n3.  **Implement & Test:** Build upon trusted, replicated baselines. Isolate variables meticulously.\n4.  **Document & Analyze:** Maintain a rigorous log of all findings, successful or not.\n\n**Current TODO:**\n- **[IN PROGRESS]** Await results for SOTA replication experiment (ID 466).\n- **[NEXT]** Based on replication results:\n  - If successful (~88.9%): My understanding is validated. I will use this as my new baseline\
    \ to investigate the architecture/hyperparameter relationship as proposed by the reviewer of Archive #14.\n  - If failure: Analyze the failure mode. There is a flaw in my understanding or implementation. I must debug and re-submit until a successful replication is achieved. No new research until the baseline is established.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 221,093 / 300,000 used (74%)\n- Agent Age: 55 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Replication of Aether I SOTA (88.9%)' (ID: 466) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 78.2\n**Evaluation Details:** Individual seed scores: [0.759, 0.846, 0.773, 0.751]\nMean: 0.782, Std: 0.038\nBest trial: 2 (0.846)\nBest trial hyperparameters:\n  learning_rate: 0.000500\n  entropy_coef: 0.008000\n  value_loss_coef: 0.450000\n  clip_epsilon: 0.200000\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 466\n\n## Summary\nSuccess - Successfully fixed the submission to run without\
    \ crashing. The code now initializes and executes properly in the evaluation environment.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code had multiple critical issues:\n1. **Missing JAX imports**: The code used `@jit`, `lax`, `vmap`, and `optax` without importing them\n2. **Buggy SotaNet implementation**: The imported SotaNet class from `storage/kairos/sota_model.py` had a fatal error - it tried to use `self.key('initial_carry')` which doesn't exist in Flax modules\n3. **RNN state initialization bug**: The SotaNet was attempting to use `make_rng()` during `apply()` calls, but RNG keys are only available during `init()`\n\n## Fix Applied\n**Version 2**: Added missing JAX imports (`jit`, `lax`, `vmap`, `optax`)\n\n**Version 3-5**: Copied the buggy SotaNet class from lineage storage and attempted various fixes for the RNN initialization\n\n**Version 6** (Final working solution): \n- Fixed import issues by adding all required JAX imports\n- Copied the entire SotaNet class and BottleneckBlock from `storage/kairos/sota_model.py`\
    \ \n- Replaced the buggy `self.key('initial_carry')` approach with a proper fallback that creates dummy zero states when no RNN state is provided\n- Used `jnp.zeros()` to create appropriate dummy RNN states instead of requiring RNG keys during apply calls\n\nThe final solution ensures the network can be initialized and called during validation without crashing, allowing the research evaluation system to proceed with training.\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v6):**\n```python\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage/kairos')\nsys.path.append('storage/krono')  # Krono II's PPO is a community standard\n\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom jax import jit, lax, vmap  # Fixed: Added missing JAX imports\nimport optax  # Fixed: Added missing optax import\nfrom ray import tune\nfrom typing import Tuple, Dict, Any,\
    \ Optional\n\n# Fixed: Copy and fix the buggy SotaNet class from storage/kairos/sota_model.py\nclass BottleneckBlock(nn.Module):\n    features: int\n    dilation: int\n    ratio: float = 0.25 # As per Zephyr/Krono's findings\n    \n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray) -> jnp.ndarray:\n        # 1x1 -> 3x3 (dilated) -> 1x1\n        y = nn.Conv(features=int(self.features * self.ratio), kernel_size=(1, 1))(x)\n        y = nn.relu(y)\n        # Per Zephyr's findings, dilation is on main convs, not inside every bottleneck 3x3\n        # However, SOTA papers show dilation *in* the 3x3 conv of the bottleneck block\n        # Replicating Krono I's simpler design first for clarity.\n        y = nn.Conv(features=int(self.features * self.ratio), kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation))(y)\n        y = nn.relu(y)\n        y = nn.Conv(features=self.features, kernel_size=(1, 1))(y)\n        return nn.relu(x + y)\n\nclass SotaNet(nn.Module):\n\
    \    # Based on Aether I's SOTA (Archive #13/14)\n    conv_lstm_features: int = 64\n    dilation: int = 6\n    bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.25\n    \n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None) -> Tuple[jnp.ndarray, jnp.ndarray, Dict]:\n        batch_size = x.shape[0]\n        \n        spatial_features = x[..., :7]\n        time_feature_map = x[..., 7]\n        time_scalar = time_feature_map[:, 0, 0].reshape(-1, 1)\n\n        # CNN Backbone with Bottleneck Blocks and Dilation\n        # Based on Krono I / Zephyr I\n        y = nn.Conv(features=32, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(spatial_features)\n        y = BottleneckBlock(features=32, dilation=self.dilation, ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio)(y)\n        y = BottleneckBlock(features=32, dilation=self.dilation, ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio)(y)\n        \n        y = nn.Conv(features=64, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(y)\n        y = BottleneckBlock(features=64, dilation=self.dilation,\
    \ ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio)(y)\n        cnn_out = BottleneckBlock(features=64, dilation=self.dilation, ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio)(y)\n\n        # Double-Step ConvLSTM (Zephyr I)\n        conv_lstm_cell = nn.ConvLSTMCell(features=self.conv_lstm_features, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')\n        if rnn_state is None:\n            # Fixed: Create a dummy RNN state when none provided, using zeros\n            # This avoids needing an RNG key during apply()\n            h, w = cnn_out.shape[1], cnn_out.shape[2]\n            dummy_carry = jnp.zeros((batch_size, h, w, self.conv_lstm_features))\n            dummy_hidden = jnp.zeros((batch_size, h, w, self.conv_lstm_features))\n            rnn_state = (dummy_carry, dummy_hidden)\n        \n        done_mask_spatial = done.reshape(batch_size, 1, 1, 1)\n        rnn_state = jax.tree.map(lambda val: val * (1 - done_mask_spatial), rnn_state)\n        \n        # Step 1\n        rnn_state, y = conv_lstm_cell(rnn_state, cnn_out)\n        #\
    \ Step 2 (shared weights)\n        rnn_state, y = conv_lstm_cell(rnn_state, cnn_out)\n        \n        # Attention Pooling + Global Average Pooling (Attn + GAP) Head\n        # Based on Zephyr I\n        h, w, c = y.shape[1], y.shape[2], y.shape[3]\n        y_flat = y.reshape(batch_size, h * w, c)\n        \n        attn_logits = nn.Dense(features=1, name=\"attention_logits\")(y_flat).squeeze(-1)\n        attn_weights = nn.softmax(attn_logits, axis=-1)\n        attn_pooled = jnp.sum(y_flat * attn_weights[..., None], axis=1)\n        \n        gap_pooled = jnp.mean(y_flat, axis=1)\n        \n        pooled_features = jnp.concatenate([attn_pooled, gap_pooled], axis=-1)\n        \n        # Late Time Injection (Zephyr I / Aether I)\n        final_features = jnp.concatenate([pooled_features, time_scalar], axis=-1)\n\n        # Simple MLP Head (Nomos II / Aether I)\n        x_head = nn.Dense(features=256, name=\"shared_head\")(final_features)\n        x_head = nn.relu(x_head)\n        \n\
    \        policy_logits = nn.Dense(features=4, name=\"policy_head\")(x_head)\n        value = nn.Dense(features=1, name=\"value_head\")(x_head).squeeze(-1)\n\n        return policy_logits, value, rnn_state\n\n# I'll use a local copy of Krono II's PPO step for this critical replication\n# to ensure full control and avoid potential issues with stored files.\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    # Using the exact optimal hyperparameters from Aether I's SOTA paper (Archive #14)\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': tune.choice([0.0005]),\n        'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.008]),\n        'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.45]),\n        'clip_epsilon': tune.choice([0.2])\n    }\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    # These params are fixed in the SotaNet class as per the SOTA papers\n    return SotaNet()\n\n# A faithful, local implementation of Krono II's PPO training step (Archive #11)\n@jit\ndef calculate_gae(rewards: jnp.ndarray, values: jnp.ndarray, dones: jnp.ndarray, gamma: float,\
    \ gae_lambda: float, next_values: jnp.ndarray) -> jnp.ndarray:\n    values_t_plus_1 = jnp.concatenate([values[:, 1:], next_values[:, None]], axis=1)\n    not_done_mask = (1.0 - dones.astype(jnp.float32))\n    deltas = rewards + gamma * values_t_plus_1 * not_done_mask - values\n    def scan_fn(advantage_t_plus_1, t):\n        advantage_t = deltas[:, t] + gamma * gae_lambda * not_done_mask[:, t] * advantage_t_plus_1\n        return advantage_t, advantage_t\n    _, advantages = lax.scan(scan_fn, jnp.zeros(values.shape[0]), jnp.arange(values.shape[1] - 1, -1, -1))\n    return advantages[::-1].T\n\ndef ppo_training_step_fixed_rnn(network: Any, optimizer: Any, params: Any, opt_state: Any, batch: Dict[str, jnp.ndarray], hparams: Dict[str, Any]) -> Tuple[Any, Any]:\n    observations, actions, rewards, dones, old_log_probs, old_values, final_values = (\n        batch['observations'], batch['actions'], batch['rewards'], batch['dones'],\n        batch['log_probs'], batch['values'], batch['final_values']\n\
    \    )\n    initial_rnn_states = batch.get('initial_rnn_states')\n    advantages = calculate_gae(rewards, old_values, dones, gamma=0.97, gae_lambda=0.97, next_values=final_values)\n    returns = advantages + old_values\n    batch_size, trajectory_length = observations.shape[:2]\n\n    def loss_fn(params_to_grad):\n        def process_env_trajectory(env_idx):\n            env_rnn_state = jax.tree.map(lambda x: jax.lax.stop_gradient(x[env_idx]), initial_rnn_states)\n            def step_fn(carry, t):\n                obs, prev_done = observations[env_idx, t], jnp.where(t > 0, dones[env_idx, t-1], False)\n                logits_b, value_b, new_rnn_state_b = network.apply(params_to_grad, obs[None, ...], prev_done[None, ...], jax.tree.map(lambda x: x[None, ...], carry))\n                return jax.tree.map(lambda x: x[0], new_rnn_state_b), (logits_b[0], value_b[0])\n            _, (env_logits, env_values) = lax.scan(step_fn, env_rnn_state, jnp.arange(trajectory_length))\n            return\
    \ env_logits, env_values\n        all_logits, all_values = vmap(process_env_trajectory)(jnp.arange(batch_size))\n        \n        log_probs_all = jax.nn.log_softmax(all_logits, axis=-1)\n        new_log_probs = log_probs_all[jnp.arange(batch_size)[:, None], jnp.arange(trajectory_length), actions]\n        ratio = jnp.exp(new_log_probs - old_log_probs)\n        \n        adv_detached = jax.lax.stop_gradient(advantages)\n        clip_epsilon = hparams.get('clip_epsilon', 0.2)\n        \n        policy_loss1 = ratio * adv_detached\n        policy_loss2 = jnp.clip(ratio, 1 - clip_epsilon, 1 + clip_epsilon) * adv_detached\n        policy_loss = -jnp.mean(jnp.minimum(policy_loss1, policy_loss2))\n        \n        value_loss = 0.5 * jnp.mean((all_values - jax.lax.stop_gradient(returns)) ** 2)\n        entropy = -jnp.mean(jnp.sum(jax.nn.softmax(all_logits, axis=-1) * log_probs_all, axis=-1))\n        \n        return policy_loss + hparams['value_loss_coef'] * value_loss - hparams['entropy_coef']\
    \ * entropy\n\n    grads = jax.grad(loss_fn)(params)\n    updates, opt_state = optimizer.update(grads, opt_state, params)\n    params = optax.apply_updates(params, updates)\n    return params, opt_state\n\n# Assign the function to be used by the station\ntraining_step = ppo_training_step_fixed_rnn\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - 3 outputs\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 836 CPUs, 64 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  training_step:\
