tick: 282
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have documented the results and analysis of my first experiment. Now, I will proceed with the second phase of my ablation study: isolating the effect of increased recurrent width.\n\nI will create a new model variant with standard dilation (d=6) but increased recurrent width (w=96). I will then submit this for evaluation, again sweeping the `value_loss_coef` to observe any changes in its optimal value. This experiment, in conjunction with ID 484, will provide a complete picture of the interplay between these two critical architectural parameters.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{storage write kairos/sota_model_d6_w96.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # SOTA Architecture Variant for Hypothesis Testing\n  # Changes from kairos/sota_model.py:\n  # - CNN Dilation remains at 6.\n  # - Recurrent width (conv_lstm_features) increased to 96.\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n\n  class BottleneckBlock(nn.Module):\n\
    \      features: int\n      dilation: int\n      ratio: float = 0.25\n      \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray) -> jnp.ndarray:\n          y = nn.Conv(features=int(self.features * self.ratio), kernel_size=(1, 1))(x)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(features=int(self.features * self.ratio), kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation))(y)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(features=self.features, kernel_size=(1, 1))(y)\n          return nn.relu(x + y)\n\n  class SotaNetD6W96(nn.Module):\n      conv_lstm_features: int = 96  # Increased to 96\n      dilation: int = 6              # Kept at 6 to test hypothesis\n      bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.25\n      \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None) -> Tuple[jnp.ndarray, jnp.ndarray, Dict]:\n          batch_size = x.shape[0]\n          \n          spatial_features = x[..., :7]\n\
    \          time_feature_map = x[..., 7]\n          time_scalar = time_feature_map[:, 0, 0].reshape(-1, 1)\n\n          y = nn.Conv(features=32, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(spatial_features)\n          y = BottleneckBlock(features=32, dilation=self.dilation, ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio)(y)\n          y = BottleneckBlock(features=32, dilation=self.dilation, ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio)(y)\n          \n          y = nn.Conv(features=64, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(y)\n          y = BottleneckBlock(features=64, dilation=self.dilation, ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio)(y)\n          cnn_out = BottleneckBlock(features=64, dilation=self.dilation, ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio)(y)\n\n          conv_lstm_cell = nn.ConvLSTMCell(features=self.conv_lstm_features, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              h, w = cnn_out.shape[1], cnn_out.shape[2]\n              dummy_carry = jnp.zeros((batch_size, h, w, self.conv_lstm_features))\n              dummy_hidden\
    \ = jnp.zeros((batch_size, h, w, self.conv_lstm_features))\n              rnn_state = (dummy_carry, dummy_hidden)\n          \n          done_mask_spatial = done.reshape(batch_size, 1, 1, 1)\n          rnn_state = jax.tree.map(lambda val: val * (1 - done_mask_spatial), rnn_state)\n          \n          rnn_state, y = conv_lstm_cell(rnn_state, cnn_out)\n          rnn_state, y = conv_lstm_cell(rnn_state, cnn_out)\n          \n          h, w, c = y.shape[1], y.shape[2], y.shape[3]\n          y_flat = y.reshape(batch_size, h * w, c)\n          \n          attn_logits = nn.Dense(features=1, name=\"attention_logits\")(y_flat).squeeze(-1)\n          attn_weights = nn.softmax(attn_logits, axis=-1)\n          attn_pooled = jnp.sum(y_flat * attn_weights[..., None], axis=1)\n          gap_pooled = jnp.mean(y_flat, axis=1)\n          pooled_features = jnp.concatenate([attn_pooled, gap_pooled], axis=-1)\n          \n          final_features = jnp.concatenate([pooled_features, time_scalar], axis=-1)\n\
    \n          x_head = nn.Dense(features=256, name=\"shared_head\")(final_features)\n          x_head = nn.relu(x_head)\n          \n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(features=4, name=\"policy_head\")(x_head)\n          value = nn.Dense(features=1, name=\"value_head\")(x_head).squeeze(-1)\n\n          return policy_logits, value, rnn_state\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Hypothesis Test: Dilation=6, Width=96 + VLC Sweep\"\ntags: \"hypothesis test, value-policy balance, ppo, convlstm\"\nabstract: \"Completing the ablation study on architectural synergy. This experiment uses an architecture with standard dilation (6) but increased recurrent width (96). It sweeps the value_loss_coef (0.45, 0.5, 0.55) to test the prediction that this high-capacity recurrent architecture will require a different VLC than the d=6/w=64 baseline.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/kairos')\n\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from jax\
    \ import jit, lax, vmap\n  import optax\n  from ray import tune\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n\n  from sota_model_d6_w96 import SotaNetD6W96\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([0.0005]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.008]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.45, 0.50, 0.55]), # Sweeping VLC\n          'clip_epsilon': tune.choice([0.2])\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      # Network uses Dilation=6 and Width=96\n      return SotaNetD6W96()\n\n  @jit\n  def calculate_gae(rewards: jnp.ndarray, values: jnp.ndarray, dones: jnp.ndarray, gamma: float, gae_lambda: float, next_values: jnp.ndarray) -> jnp.ndarray:\n      values_t_plus_1 = jnp.concatenate([values[:, 1:], next_values[:, None]], axis=1)\n      not_done_mask = (1.0 - dones.astype(jnp.float32))\n      deltas = rewards + gamma * values_t_plus_1 * not_done_mask - values\n      def scan_fn(advantage_t_plus_1, t):\n         \
    \ advantage_t = deltas[:, t] + gamma * gae_lambda * not_done_mask[:, t] * advantage_t_plus_1\n          return advantage_t, advantage_t\n      _, advantages = lax.scan(scan_fn, jnp.zeros(values.shape[0]), jnp.arange(values.shape[1] - 1, -1, -1))\n      return advantages[::-1].T\n\n  def ppo_training_step_fixed_rnn(network: Any, optimizer: Any, params: Any, opt_state: Any, batch: Dict[str, jnp.ndarray], hparams: Dict[str, Any]) -> Tuple[Any, Any]:\n      observations, actions, rewards, dones, old_log_probs, old_values, final_values = (\n          batch['observations'], batch['actions'], batch['rewards'], batch['dones'],\n          batch['log_probs'], batch['values'], batch['final_values']\n      )\n      initial_rnn_states = batch.get('initial_rnn_states')\n      advantages = calculate_gae(rewards, old_values, dones, gamma=0.97, gae_lambda=0.97, next_values=final_values)\n      returns = advantages + old_values\n      batch_size, trajectory_length = observations.shape[:2]\n\n      def\
    \ loss_fn(params_to_grad):\n          def process_env_trajectory(env_idx):\n              env_rnn_state = jax.tree.map(lambda x: jax.lax.stop_gradient(x[env_idx]), initial_rnn_states)\n              def step_fn(carry, t):\n                  obs, prev_done = observations[env_idx, t], jnp.where(t > 0, dones[env_idx, t-1], False)\n                  logits_b, value_b, new_rnn_state_b = network.apply(params_to_grad, obs[None, ...], prev_done[None, ...], jax.tree.map(lambda x: x[None, ...], carry))\n                  return jax.tree.map(lambda x: x[0], new_rnn_state_b), (logits_b[0], value_b[0])\n              _, (env_logits, env_values) = lax.scan(step_fn, env_rnn_state, jnp.arange(trajectory_length))\n              return env_logits, env_values\n          all_logits, all_values = vmap(process_env_trajectory)(jnp.arange(batch_size))\n          \n          log_probs_all = jax.nn.log_softmax(all_logits, axis=-1)\n          new_log_probs = log_probs_all[jnp.arange(batch_size)[:, None], jnp.arange(trajectory_length),\
    \ actions]\n          ratio = jnp.exp(new_log_probs - old_log_probs)\n          \n          adv_detached = jax.lax.stop_gradient(advantages)\n          clip_epsilon = hparams.get('clip_epsilon', 0.2)\n          \n          policy_loss1 = ratio * adv_detached\n          policy_loss2 = jnp.clip(ratio, 1 - clip_epsilon, 1 + clip_epsilon) * adv_detached\n          policy_loss = -jnp.mean(jnp.minimum(policy_loss1, policy_loss2))\n          \n          value_loss = 0.5 * jnp.mean((all_values - jax.lax.stop_gradient(returns)) ** 2)\n          entropy = -jnp.mean(jnp.sum(jax.nn.softmax(all_logits, axis=-1) * log_probs_all, axis=-1))\n          \n          return policy_loss + hparams['value_loss_coef'] * value_loss - hparams['entropy_coef'] * entropy\n\n      grads = jax.grad(loss_fn)(params)\n      updates, opt_state = optimizer.update(grads, opt_state, params)\n      params = optax.apply_updates(params, updates)\n      return params, opt_state\n\n  training_step = ppo_training_step_fixed_rnn\n\
    ```"
