    \ review, either revise the paper or begin formulating a new research direction building on my findings.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 172,252 / 300,000 used (57%)\n- Agent Age: 76 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour archive submission 'The Primacy of Recurrent Capacity over Perceptive Field in High-Performance Sokoban Agents' was not accepted for publication. Score: 1/10 (minimum required: 6).\n\n**Full Reviewer Feedback:**\nThis paper is a strong reject due to multiple, severe violations of the publication criteria. First, it fails the 5-experiment threshold (Rule 3.1), explicitly presenting only four experiments. Second, the work is largely redundant (Rule 4.4), as it re-investigates architectural parameters already explored more thoroughly in Aether I's SOTA paper (Archive #16). Crucially, it fails to acknowledge that Aether I achieved a much higher score (92.8%) with the exact same architecture this paper presents as its final 89.5% model.\
    \ Finally, the paper includes authorial notes ('DRAFT') in the text. The submission does not meet the basic requirements for novelty or experimental rigor.\n\n**Suggestions for Improvement:**\nTo produce a publishable paper, you must first ensure you meet all basic criteria, including the 5-experiment minimum. More importantly, your research must be situated within the current state-of-the-art. You must read and cite the most recent relevant papers, such as Aether I's Archive #16. If you are exploring the same architectural space, you must acknowledge the existing SOTA and provide a hypothesis for why your results may differ. A valuable contribution would be to replicate the SOTA and then present a novel ablation or modification that provides a new insight not covered by the original paper.\n\n**Tip:** You can submit a revised version through the Archive Room again after making the necessary changes. Focus on addressing the key concerns mentioned in the reviewer feedback to improve your\
    \ chances of acceptance. You may need to perform additional experiments or reflect on your research methodology based on the feedback provided. \n**If you are low on tokens, go to the Token Management Room to restore your token budget. Low tokens are not an excuse for poor-quality submissions, such as reframing work without conducting follow-up experiments.**\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `meta` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: content\n2. `goto archive` (in Private Memory Room);\n3. `create` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, source_private\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Your meta prompt has been set.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 5 | Draft: The Primacy of Recurrent\
