tick: 296
role: model
parts:
- text: "**Reflection Tick 4 / 5: Designing the Final Output and Interpretation Framework**\n\nThe final step of the probe design is to define the output format. The `test()` function should produce a clear, concise, and easily parsable report. A structured printout is superior to a simple return value, as it allows for immediate analysis without needing to review the full logs.\n\n**Output Format:**\nI will design the output as a Markdown-formatted table printed to STDOUT. This is both human-readable and structured.\n\n```\n# Mechanistic Probe: Architectural Comparison\n\n## --- Model A: d=7 / w=64 (Bottlenecked) ---\n| Metric                  | Step 1   | Step 2   |\n|-------------------------|----------|----------|\n| Gate Saturation (>|4.0|)| X.XXXX % | Y.YYYY % |\n| Mean Spatial Variance   | A.AAAA   | B.BBBB   |\n\n## --- Model B: d=6 / w=96 (High-Performing) ---\n| Metric                  | Step 1   | Step 2   |\n|-------------------------|----------|----------|\n| Gate Saturation\
    \ (>|4.0|)| Z.ZZZZ % | W.WWWW % |\n| Mean Spatial Variance   | C.CCCC   | D.DDDD   |\n\n## --- Interpretation ---\n- [Auto-generated interpretation statement based on the results]\n```\n\n**Interpretation Logic:**\nThe `test()` function will include a simple conditional logic block to print a qualitative summary of the findings, directly testing my hypothesis.\n\n```python\n# In the test() function, after computing all metrics...\n\nprint(\"## --- Interpretation ---\")\n\n# Compare Gate Saturation\nsaturation_a = ... # (mean of step 1 & 2 for model A)\nsaturation_b = ... # (mean of step 1 & 2 for model B)\nif saturation_a > saturation_b * 1.5: # Require a significant difference (e.g., 50% higher)\n    print(\"- CONFIRMED: Bottlenecked model (A) shows significantly higher gate saturation than the high-performing model (B).\")\nelse:\n    print(\"- UNCONFIRMED: Gate saturation is not significantly different between models.\")\n\n# Compare Spatial Variance\nvariance_a = ... # (mean of step\
    \ 1 & 2 for model A)\nvariance_b = ... # (mean of step 1 & 2 for model B)\nif variance_a < variance_b * 0.75: # Require a significant difference (e.g., 25% lower)\n    print(\"- CONFIRMED: Bottlenecked model (A) shows significantly lower mean spatial variance, suggesting representational collapse.\")\nelse:\n    print(\"- UNCONFIRMED: Mean spatial variance is not significantly different between models.\")\n\nreturn \"Probe complete. See report above.\"\n```\n\n**Final `submission.py` Structure:**\nThe final submission file for this probe will be self-contained.\n1.  Import necessary libraries.\n2.  Define the `ProbeConvLSTMCell`.\n3.  Define the `SotaNet` architecture, modified to accept the `ProbeConvLSTMCell`.\n4.  Define the `test()` function, which will:\n    a. Instantiate the two model configurations.\n    b. Extract intermediate data using `capture_intermediates`.\n    c. Compute the Gate Saturation and Spatial Variance metrics.\n    d. Print the formatted Markdown report.\n \
    \   e. Print the automated interpretation.\n5.  Crucially, it will *not* define `create_network` or `training_step` for the main evaluation, ensuring only the `test()` function runs.\n\nThis comprehensive design provides a clear plan for a rigorous, self-contained, and easily interpretable mechanistic probe. It will produce a single, clear artifact that either confirms or refutes my hypothesis about the internal dynamics of these architectures."
