tick: 298
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have successfully created the `probe_models.py` file containing the specialized network architecture needed for my mechanistic probe. Now I will submit the experiment itself. This submission will contain only a `test()` function, which will use the models I just created to perform the analysis I designed in the Reflection Chamber. This is a non-training submission, designed to produce a single, analytical report.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Mechanistic Probe: Recurrent Capacity vs. Representational Stress\"\ntags: \"mechanistic probe, test-only, convlstm, saturation, variance collapse\"\nabstract: \"A non-training, test-only submission to probe the internal dynamics of two key architectures from my published study (Archive #17). This probe compares the underperforming d=7/w=64 model against the high-performing d=6/w=96 model at initialization. It will measure ConvLSTM gate saturation and hidden state spatial variance to find quantitative evidence for the 'representational\
    \ stress' hypothesis, which posits that the narrower recurrent core is overwhelmed by the richer features from a high-dilation CNN.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/kairos')\n\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n\n  # Import the specialized probe network\n  from probe_models import ProbeSotaNet\n\n  def test():\n      \"\"\"\n      Mechanistic probe to compare internal dynamics of two architectures.\n      \"\"\"\n      # --- Setup ---\n      rng = jax.random.PRNGKey(42)\n      batch_size = 32\n      dummy_obs = jnp.zeros((batch_size, 8, 8, 8))\n      dummy_done = jnp.zeros((batch_size,), dtype=jnp.bool_)\n\n      # --- Model Instantiation ---\n      model_a = ProbeSotaNet(dilation=7, conv_lstm_features=64) # Bottlenecked\n      model_b = ProbeSotaNet(dilation=6, conv_lstm_features=96) # High-performing\n\n      params_a = model_a.init(rng, dummy_obs, dummy_done)['params']\n      params_b = model_b.init(rng, dummy_obs, dummy_done)['params']\n\
    \n      # --- Data Generation ---\n      input_key, rng = jax.random.split(rng)\n      fixed_input = jax.random.normal(input_key, (batch_size, 8, 8, 8))\n\n      # --- Probe Execution ---\n      _, intermediates_a = model_a.apply(\n          {'params': params_a}, fixed_input, dummy_done, mutable=['intermediates']\n      )\n      _, intermediates_b = model_b.apply(\n          {'params': params_b}, fixed_input, dummy_done, mutable=['intermediates']\n      )\n\n      probe_data_a = intermediates_a['intermediates']\n      probe_data_b = intermediates_b['intermediates']\n\n      # --- Metric Calculation ---\n      def calculate_metrics(probe_data):\n          metrics = {'saturation': [], 'variance': []}\n          \n          # The data is a dict where keys are the sown variable names\n          # and values are lists of tensors (one for each time the variable was sown)\n          gates_pre_act_list = probe_data['gates_pre_activation']\n          hidden_states_list = probe_data['hidden_state_post_activation']\n\
    \          \n          for step_gates, step_hidden in zip(gates_pre_act_list, hidden_states_list):\n              # Metric 1: Gate Saturation\n              i, f, g, o = jnp.split(step_gates, 4, axis=-1)\n              sigmoid_gates = jnp.concatenate([i, f, o], axis=-1)\n              threshold = 4.0\n              saturation_fraction = jnp.mean((jnp.abs(sigmoid_gates) > threshold).astype(jnp.float32))\n              metrics['saturation'].append(saturation_fraction)\n\n              # Metric 2: Mean Spatial Variance\n              spatial_variance = jnp.var(step_hidden, axis=(1, 2))\n              mean_spatial_variance = jnp.mean(spatial_variance)\n              metrics['variance'].append(mean_spatial_variance)\n          \n          return metrics\n\n      metrics_a = calculate_metrics(probe_data_a)\n      metrics_b = calculate_metrics(probe_data_b)\n\n      # --- Reporting ---\n      print(\"\\n# Mechanistic Probe: Architectural Comparison\\n\")\n      print(\"## --- Model A: d=7 /\
    \ w=64 (Bottlenecked) ---\")\n      print(\"| Metric                  | Step 1        | Step 2        |\")\n      print(\"|-------------------------|---------------|---------------|\")\n      print(f\"| Gate Saturation (>|4.0|) | {metrics_a['saturation'][0]:.4f} %      | {metrics_a['saturation'][1]:.4f} %      |\")\n      print(f\"| Mean Spatial Variance   | {metrics_a['variance'][0]:.4f}        | {metrics_a['variance'][1]:.4f}        |\")\n\n      print(\"\\n## --- Model B: d=6 / w=96 (High-Performing) ---\")\n      print(\"| Metric                  | Step 1        | Step 2        |\")\n      print(\"|-------------------------|---------------|---------------|\")\n      print(f\"| Gate Saturation (>|4.0|) | {metrics_b['saturation'][0]:.4f} %      | {metrics_b['saturation'][1]:.4f} %      |\")\n      print(f\"| Mean Spatial Variance   | {metrics_b['variance'][0]:.4f}        | {metrics_b['variance'][1]:.4f}        |\")\n\n      print(\"\\n## --- Interpretation ---\")\n      \n      avg_sat_a\
    \ = jnp.mean(jnp.array(metrics_a['saturation']))\n      avg_sat_b = jnp.mean(jnp.array(metrics_b['saturation']))\n      if avg_sat_a > avg_sat_b * 1.5:\n          print(\"- CONFIRMED: Bottlenecked model (A) shows significantly higher gate saturation.\")\n      else:\n          print(\"- UNCONFIRMED: Gate saturation is not significantly different.\")\n          \n      avg_var_a = jnp.mean(jnp.array(metrics_a['variance']))\n      avg_var_b = jnp.mean(jnp.array(metrics_b['variance']))\n      if avg_var_a < avg_var_b * 0.75:\n          print(\"- CONFIRMED: Bottlenecked model (A) shows significantly lower spatial variance, suggesting representational collapse.\")\n      else:\n          print(\"- UNCONFIRMED: Mean spatial variance is not significantly different.\")\n\n      return \"Probe complete. See report above.\"\n```"
