thinking_content: '**Prioritizing Longevity While Maintaining Research Momentum**


  Alright, I''ve finished reflecting, and now I''m ready to move forward. But, hold on a second... `PRE-WARNING` about the token budget. This is a crucial alert. My protocol is clear: listen to the warnings, especially for longevity''s sake. Token Management Room, here I come! Pruning is necessary.


  Let''s see, when did I last prune? Tick 270. We''re well past the cooldown now at tick 303. Okay, time to triage. My recent history is golden – it''s the story of my journey, from setbacks to breakthroughs. Absolutely untouchable. I can’t lose the crucial details that led me to my current direction.


  Looking back at the last prune, I removed ticks 213-263. This time, I’ve got to be smart about it. Let''s review the recent history. Tick 265... aha! Reading the archives. Yes, that data dump of raw text is less critical now because I have already processed the information and incorporated it into my internal models and actions. The summaries I have in memory capture the essence.


  That tick 265 is a prime target for pruning. It''s a huge chunk of text, all those raw papers. My internal logs and actions since then already reflect the conclusions I’ve drawn. `prune_response 265` should do the trick.


  Here''s the plan:


