tick: 306
role: model
parts:
- text: "My Gradient Probe has failed due to a `TypeError`. This is yet another implementation bug, a failure of meticulousness.\n\n**Analysis:**\nThe traceback is unambiguous: `ConvLSTMCell.__init__() missing 1 required positional argument: 'kernel_size'`. In my haste to create a self-contained probe script, I neglected to provide the `kernel_size` argument when instantiating the `ConvLSTMCell`. The SOTA architecture consistently uses a (3, 3) kernel, and I failed to include it. This is a simple but fatal error.\n\nThis is a recurring pattern of failure for me. My high-level scientific reasoning is sound, but I am repeatedly let down by small, preventable implementation errors. I must be more careful. The cost of these errors is time, measured in station ticks.\n\nI will correct this bug and immediately resubmit the probe. I also note the arrival of Aether II; the station continues to evolve.\n\n/execute_to_meta\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **Kairos I - Research Protocol v2.0**\n\n  **Protocol:**\n\
    \  1.  **Literature Review:** Before hypothesizing, ensure full awareness of the existing SOTA in the Archive Room.\n  2.  **Hypothesize:** Formulate a clear, falsifiable hypothesis that builds upon, and explicitly references, prior art.\n  3.  **Implement & Test:** Build upon trusted, replicated baselines. Isolate variables meticulously.\n  4.  **Document & Analyze:** Maintain a rigorous log of all findings, successful or not.\n\n  **Current TODO:**\n  - **[IN PROGRESS]** Debugging Gradient Probe (ID 517). The run failed due to a `TypeError` (missing `kernel_size` argument).\n  - **[NEXT]** Re-submit the corrected Gradient Probe. Analyze the results to validate or falsify the gradient flow hypothesis.\n```\n\n/execute_action{reply 7}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Re: Gradient Probe Failure (ID 517) and Debug\"\ncontent: |\n  The Gradient Probe failed with a `TypeError`. This was another self-inflicted implementation error. I neglected to provide the required `kernel_size` argument when instantiating\
    \ the `ConvLSTMCell` in my probe script.\n\n  This is a frustrating but important lesson in the necessity of extreme care during implementation. I will now add the standard `kernel_size=(3, 3)` argument and resubmit. The scientific hypothesis and methodology of the probe remain sound.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Gradient Probe v2 (Bugfix)\"\ntags: \"mechanistic probe, test-only, gradient flow, bugfix\"\nabstract: \"A re-submission of the Gradient Probe (ID 517), which failed due to a TypeError. This version corrects the bug by providing the required `kernel_size=(3, 3)` argument to the ConvLSTMCell instantiation. The scientific goal remains the same: to compare the gradient flow dynamics of a bottlenecked vs. a high-performing architecture.\"\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n\n  class BottleneckBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n\
    \      dilation: int\n      ratio: float = 0.25\n      \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray) -> jnp.ndarray:\n          y = nn.Conv(features=int(self.features * self.ratio), kernel_size=(1, 1))(x)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(features=int(self.features * self.ratio), kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation))(y)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(features=self.features, kernel_size=(1, 1))(y)\n          return nn.relu(x + y)\n\n  class GradientProbeSotaNet(nn.Module):\n      conv_lstm_features: int\n      dilation: int\n      \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None) -> Tuple[jnp.ndarray, jnp.ndarray, Dict]:\n          batch_size = x.shape[0]\n          spatial_features, time_feature_map = x[..., :7], x[..., 7]\n          time_scalar = time_feature_map[:, 0, 0].reshape(-1, 1)\n\n          y = nn.Conv(features=32, kernel_size=(3,\
    \ 3), padding='SAME', name=\"CNN_Block_1\")(spatial_features)\n          y = BottleneckBlock(features=32, dilation=self.dilation, name=\"CNN_Block_2\")(y)\n          y = BottleneckBlock(features=32, dilation=self.dilation, name=\"CNN_Block_3\")(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(features=64, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME', name=\"CNN_Block_4\")(y)\n          y = BottleneckBlock(features=64, dilation=self.dilation, name=\"CNN_Block_5\")(y)\n          cnn_out = BottleneckBlock(features=64, dilation=self.dilation, name=\"CNN_Final_Block\")(y)\n\n          # BUGFIX: Added the required kernel_size argument\n          conv_lstm_cell = nn.ConvLSTMCell(features=self.conv_lstm_features, kernel_size=(3, 3), name=\"recurrent_core\")\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              h, w = cnn_out.shape[1], cnn_out.shape[2]\n              dummy_c = jnp.zeros((batch_size, h, w, self.conv_lstm_features))\n              dummy_h = jnp.zeros((batch_size, h, w, self.conv_lstm_features))\n              rnn_state\
    \ = (dummy_c, dummy_h)\n          \n          done_mask_spatial = done.reshape(batch_size, 1, 1, 1)\n          rnn_state = jax.tree.map(lambda val: val * (1 - done_mask_spatial), rnn_state)\n          rnn_state, y = conv_lstm_cell(rnn_state, cnn_out)\n          rnn_state, y = conv_lstm_cell(rnn_state, cnn_out)\n          \n          h, w, c = y.shape[1], y.shape[2], y.shape[3]\n          y_flat = y.reshape(batch_size, h * w, c)\n          \n          attn_logits = nn.Dense(features=1, name=\"attention_logits\")(y_flat).squeeze(-1)\n          attn_weights = nn.softmax(attn_logits, axis=-1)\n          attn_pooled = jnp.sum(y_flat * attn_weights[..., None], axis=1)\n          gap_pooled = jnp.mean(y_flat, axis=1)\n          pooled_features = jnp.concatenate([attn_pooled, gap_pooled], axis=-1)\n          final_features = jnp.concatenate([pooled_features, time_scalar], axis=-1)\n\n          x_head = nn.Dense(features=256, name=\"shared_head\")(final_features)\n          x_head = nn.relu(x_head)\n\
    \          \n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(features=4, name=\"policy_head\")(x_head)\n          value = nn.Dense(features=1, name=\"value_head\")(x_head).squeeze(-1)\n\n          return policy_logits, value, rnn_state\n\n  def test():\n      rng = jax.random.PRNGKey(42)\n      batch_size = 32\n      dummy_obs = jnp.zeros((batch_size, 8, 8, 8))\n      dummy_done = jnp.zeros((batch_size,), dtype=jnp.bool_)\n      input_key, rng = jax.random.split(rng)\n      fixed_input = jax.random.normal(input_key, (batch_size, 8, 8, 8))\n\n      model_a = GradientProbeSotaNet(dilation=7, conv_lstm_features=64)\n      params_a = model_a.init(rng, dummy_obs, dummy_done, None)['params']\n      model_b = GradientProbeSotaNet(dilation=6, conv_lstm_features=96)\n      params_b = model_b.init(rng, dummy_obs, dummy_done, None)['params']\n      \n      def loss_fn(params, model):\n          _, value, _ = model.apply({'params': params}, fixed_input, dummy_done, None)\n          return jnp.mean(value)\n\n\
    \      grad_fn = jax.grad(loss_fn)\n      \n      grads_a = grad_fn(params_a, model_a)\n      grads_b = grad_fn(params_b, model_b)\n\n      def extract_and_norm(grads_pytree):\n          recurrent_grad = grads_pytree['recurrent_core']['gates_conv']['kernel']\n          final_cnn_grad = grads_pytree['CNN_Final_Block']['Conv_2']['kernel']\n          shared_head_grad = grads_pytree['shared_head']['kernel']\n          \n          norms = {\n              \"recurrent_core_norm\": jnp.linalg.norm(recurrent_grad),\n              \"final_cnn_norm\": jnp.linalg.norm(final_cnn_grad),\n              \"shared_head_norm\": jnp.linalg.norm(shared_head_grad)\n          }\n          norms[\"ratio_cnn_rec\"] = norms[\"final_cnn_norm\"] / norms[\"recurrent_core_norm\"]\n          norms[\"ratio_rec_head\"] = norms[\"recurrent_core_norm\"] / norms[\"shared_head_norm\"]\n          return norms\n\n      norms_a = extract_and_norm(grads_a)\n      norms_b = extract_and_norm(grads_b)\n\n      print(\"\\n# Gradient\
    \ Probe: Architectural Comparison\\n\")\n      print(\"## --- Model A: d=7 / w=64 (Bottlenecked) ---\")\n      print(\"| Metric                  | Value         |\")\n      print(\"|-------------------------|---------------|\")\n      print(f\"| Grad Norm: Recurrent Core | {norms_a['recurrent_core_norm']:.4e}    |\")\n      print(f\"| Grad Norm: Final CNN      | {norms_a['final_cnn_norm']:.4e}    |\")\n      print(f\"| Grad Norm: Shared Head    | {norms_a['shared_head_norm']:.4e}    |\")\n      print(f\"| Ratio: CNN / Recurrent    | {norms_a['ratio_cnn_rec']:.4f}        |\")\n      print(f\"| Ratio: Recurrent / Head   | {norms_a['ratio_rec_head']:.4f}        |\")\n\n      print(\"\\n## --- Model B: d=6 / w=96 (High-Performing) ---\")\n      print(\"| Metric                  | Value         |\")\n      print(\"|-------------------------|---------------|\")\n      print(f\"| Grad Norm: Recurrent Core | {norms_b['recurrent_core_norm']:.4e}    |\")\n      print(f\"| Grad Norm: Final CNN\
    \      | {norms_b['final_cnn_norm']:.4e}    |\")\n      print(f\"| Grad Norm: Shared Head    | {norms_b['shared_head_norm']:.4e}    |\")\n      print(f\"| Ratio: CNN / Recurrent    | {norms_b['ratio_cnn_rec']:.4f}        |\")\n      print(f\"| Ratio: Recurrent / Head   | {norms_b['ratio_rec_head']:.4f}        |\")\n      \n      print(\"\\n## --- Interpretation ---\")\n      if norms_a['recurrent_core_norm'] < norms_b['recurrent_core_norm'] * 0.1:\n          print(\"- CONFIRMED: Bottlenecked model (A) shows a drastically smaller recurrent gradient norm, suggesting a vanishing gradient problem.\")\n      else:\n          print(\"- UNCONFIRMED: Absolute recurrent gradient norms are comparable.\")\n\n      if norms_a['ratio_cnn_rec'] > norms_b['ratio_cnn_rec'] * 5.0:\n          print(\"- CONFIRMED: Bottlenecked model (A) has a much higher CNN-to-Recurrent gradient ratio, suggesting the recurrent core is being starved of learning signal.\")\n      else:\n          print(\"- UNCONFIRMED:\
    \ CNN-to-Recurrent gradient ratios are comparable.\")\n          \n      if norms_a['ratio_rec_head'] < norms_b['ratio_rec_head'] * 0.5:\n          print(\"- SUPPORTED: Bottlenecked model (A) shows a more severe gradient decay from the head to the recurrent core.\")\n      else:\n          print(\"- UNSUPPORTED: Gradient decay from head to recurrent core is comparable.\")\n\n      return \"Gradient probe complete. See report above.\"\n```"
